# Contributing · `guide:foundation:contributing`

Use this guide to find the repository's working rules, label forms and invariant statements. The cited text is the authority for each practice; the [record index](adr/README.md) collects the decisions (`sec:records:index`).

## Editing and checking a change · `sec:foundation:contributing-work`

Edit prose in `docs/templates` and repeated facts in `docs/inputs`, then generate the datasets and render the documents; review and commit the generated files together with their sources (`rule:foundation:editing`). The [README's editing rule](README.md) gives the commands and their exit meanings, including the write that reports refreshed files and the subsequent check that must pass. This guide is a literal template for a root Markdown document, rendered under (`dec:render:policy`) and (`cor:render:tradeoffs`).

Run `python3 -B ci/precheck.py` before the full gate, using the gate environment and explicitly prepared checker executables: it checks registrations and structural correspondence without compiling or executing tests (`rule:buildgraph:registration-precheck`). A new tracked file needs its build-graph declaration, and its labels and citations must fit the declared owners and inventories; follow the [build-graph record](adr/024-build-graph.md) for the complete registration checks.

Run `bash ci/gate.sh` from the repository root on the committed, clean tree with the tracked toolchain, Python and the linter supplied through `LINTER_BIN`; only its final `GATE-EXIT` status zero means every step passed (`gate:foundation:verification`). The pre-check does not replace this execution evidence. Keep the exact commands and requirements with their cited owners rather than copying a gate roster here.

## Labels and citations · `sec:foundation:contributing-labels`

The [label calculus](adr/001-label-calculus.md) fixes the forms in (`gram:labels:well-formed`), minting in (`inf:labels:mint`) and same-owner resolution in (`inf:labels:same-owner-citation`). Choose the kind by what the statement is, using the [kind registry](adr/002-environment-kinds.md), its relation (`sig:kinds:registry-data`) and (`inv:kinds:one-kind`); a guide, a section and a rule have different jobs.

These examples display the title's mint, a same-owner citation to it and a mention of it. They are fenced so they do not mint or cite again; the participation rule (`judg:labels:participation`) also explains why the doubled delimiters in the last example display a label without participating.

```text
Mint at this document's title:
# Contributing · `guide:foundation:contributing`

Same-owner citation from another ROOT-owned document:
Read the contributing guide (`guide:foundation:contributing`).

Mention of the label's spelling:
The displayed name is ``guide:foundation:contributing``.
```

